  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="c36a-396b-1636-26e6" name="Street Weapons" hidden="false">
      <description>Brutal gangs fight with fists and feet or easily concealed weapons. Clubs are short weapons (daggers, bludgeons, tyre irons; any long weapon counts as short). Spades are unarmed (fists, feet, brass knuckles, broken bottles); having little reach, unarmed attacks do not win drawn Exchanges against short weapons. Instead, when an unarmed attack triples the opponent's score it uses the Beat Down! rule rather than Overpower.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="0be4-00a2-d6e5-1b9f" name="Beat Down!" hidden="false">
      <description>When an attacker uses a Beat Down instead of Overpower, no additional wounds are caused. Instead the winner of the Exchange immediately receives 1 Honour Point from the loser.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="5bf1-1fd4-2b8f-5405" name="No Missile Weapons" hidden="false">
      <description>Brutal warbands may not include units of Missile Troops. Units may still buy Throwing Weapons. (Not true of Wasteland Warriors.)</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="4b10-7d57-2e55-dabb" name="Toughs" hidden="false">
      <description>Toughs are the TRIBAL Warriors under another name: they share all the usual rules, costs and Skills.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="8d0f-3f82-6780-8332" name="The Power of Oratory" hidden="false">
      <description>Once per game the Leader of a Roman mob can use an activation to give a speech and spend 1 to 3 Honour. Each Honour Point adds a figure to a unit of Toughs anywhere on the board that has lost members, never above its starting 5.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="7200-81de-f9de-fcf2" name="Faction Stronghold" hidden="false">
      <description>Units may retreat off their home side of the table toward their Faction Stronghold: the enemy cannot touch them, but they have left the battle. Draw a card for each: on a 2 to 6 the usual Blood Payment is paid (1 Honour per unit of Toughs or Hero, 2 for the Chief); otherwise none.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
